# Flutter / Dart — keep source YAML in Git, omit generated caches and lock at plugin root
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# **Commit** `pubspec.yaml` and other project YAML (`analysis_options.yaml`, etc.). That is
# the contract for versions and tooling; reviewers moderate dependency changes there.
#
# **Do not commit** the plugin root `pubspec.lock`. For published Dart *packages*, the
# lockfile is workspace-specific; consumers resolve from `pubspec.yaml`. CI can run
# `dart pub get` / `flutter pub get` to materialize packages locally (not in this repo).
#
# The **example app** is different: keep `example/pubspec.lock` tracked for reproducible
# demo/CI builds. That file is not ignored (only this root lockfile is, via `/pubspec.lock`).
#
# Reuse: for another library package in this repo, ignore `<that_package>/pubspec.lock`;
# for an application subfolder, commit its `pubspec.lock` like `example/`.

# Pub resolver cache and Dart tooling (never commit)
.dart_tool/
.packages
.pub-cache/
.pub/

# Flutter build outputs
build/

# Plugin metadata generated by `flutter pub get`
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies

# Root package only — see comment block above
/pubspec.lock

# IDE (aligns with example/.gitignore; *.iml is machine-local)
*.iml

# Coverage and misc
coverage/
.DS_Store

# Symbolication / obfuscation (Flutter template)
app.*.symbols
app.*.map.json
